a. social;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection;
d. mental and spiritual.
(3) In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government cooperates with government agencies, other regional governments and the community.
(4) Further provisions regarding procedures for services and handling of women and children from acts of violence, trafficking and exploitation as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Mayor Regulation.

